WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:03.970
-As House managers
in the Senate impeachment trial

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.238
seek to prove
that the President

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:07.206
Is a criminal
who's unfit for office,

00:00:07.206 --> 00:00:09.075
the President
is providing more evidence

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:11.644
that he's a criminal
who's unfit for office.

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:14.080
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.951
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:19.818
You might recall
that earlier this week,

00:00:19.818 --> 00:00:21.354
after a tense exchange

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:24.157
Between House managers and
President Trump's defense team,

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:25.625
Chief Justice John Roberts,

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:27.293
who's presiding
over the impeachment trial,

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:30.463
warned both sides
to observe the decorum

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:33.732
accorded to such an august body
as the United States Senate.

00:00:33.732 --> 00:00:36.469
-I think it is appropriate
at this point

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:40.940
for me to admonish
both the House managers

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:44.077
and the President's counsel,
in equal terms,

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:47.013
to remember
that they are addressing

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:49.615
the world's greatest
deliberative body.

00:00:49.615 --> 00:00:51.617
-The world's greatest
deliberative body?

00:00:51.617 --> 00:00:54.653
Are you serious?
There's better deliberation

00:00:54.653 --> 00:00:56.222
between the hosts
of "The Voice."

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:57.790
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.790 --> 00:00:59.359
This is a place
where a sitting senator

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:01.127
once brought out
a giant poster

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:03.196
of Ronald Reagan
holding a machine gun,

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:07.066
riding a velociraptor
to mock the Green New Deal

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:09.035
and where another senator,
James Inhofe,

00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:10.636
infamously held up a snowball

00:01:10.636 --> 00:01:13.206
to try to prove that
global warming isn't real.

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:15.775
It is not
a great deliberative body.

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:19.045
It's more like show-and-tell
hour at the senior center.

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:20.213
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:22.282
Also, the Senate isn't
a deliberative body,

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:24.383
because it doesn't deliberate.
It does nothing.

00:01:24.383 --> 00:01:26.886
It's where legislation passed
by the House goes to die.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:28.621
Democrats have passed
hundreds of bills

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:29.955
on everything
from the minimum wage

00:01:29.955 --> 00:01:32.325
to prescription drugs
to equal pay to voting rights,

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:33.860
and Mitch McConnell
has ignored all of it.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.628
In his office,
he separates his trash

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:37.063
into three different cans,

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:38.731
for evidence
against the President,

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:41.267
legislation passed by the House,
and plastic.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.468
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:44.270
And in this trial...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:48.141
In this trial right now,
we are very much seeing

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:50.476
at least some of the Senators
live down to

00:01:50.476 --> 00:01:52.678
the very low expectations
they've set for themselves.

00:01:52.678 --> 00:01:55.614
For example, former senator
and MSNBC contributor

00:01:55.614 --> 00:01:57.684
Claire McCaskill
expressed some concern

00:01:57.684 --> 00:02:00.152
that members of the Senate
might not be able to stay awake

00:02:00.152 --> 00:02:02.255
through the trial
and listen to the evidence

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:04.224
for long, uninterrupted periods.

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:06.259
-For Senators, this is hard,

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:08.428
because they're used to
moving constantly,

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:09.962
they're used to talking
constantly.

00:02:09.962 --> 00:02:13.665
They are not used to listening
for long periods of time.

00:02:13.665 --> 00:02:16.535
-I love how the hardest thing
to ask a senator to do

00:02:16.535 --> 00:02:19.072
is just shut the [Bleep] up
for one lousy day.

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:20.206
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:23.575
Just sit down and shut up.
It's not hard.

00:02:23.575 --> 00:02:25.845
It's irritating,
but it's not hard.

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:28.714
Also, you know who else
is used to talking and moving

00:02:28.714 --> 00:02:31.050
and has difficulty listening
for long periods of time?

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.286
Children.
We talk about senators

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:35.722
the way pre-K teachers
talk about story time.

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:37.323
"Well, they're used to
moving and talking,

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:39.425
so we only made it
halfway through

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:41.227
'Clifford Commits a Crime.'"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:42.762
But it's true.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:46.366
Senators apparently are having
a tough time doing their jobs,

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:49.335
because there have reportedly
been stretches of the trial

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:51.003
where senators
have been caught napping

00:02:51.003 --> 00:02:53.339
or missing from their desks.
And the A.P. reported today

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.441
that almost immediately,
bored and weary senators

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.743
started openly flouting
some basic guidelines.

00:02:57.743 --> 00:02:59.679
At a chamber
that prizes decorum,

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:02.314
when one of the freshman House
prosecutors stood to speak,

00:03:02.314 --> 00:03:05.384
many of the senator jurors
bolted for the cloakrooms,

00:03:05.384 --> 00:03:06.585
where their phones are stored.

00:03:06.585 --> 00:03:09.489
Oh, my God, they're like parents
at a school play

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:11.691
when someone else's kid
is onstage.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:13.992
"Okay, Tyler's part is done,
so I'm gonna go

00:03:13.992 --> 00:03:16.128
warm up the car
for three hours."

00:03:16.128 --> 00:03:18.264
Also read the first part
of that sentence again.

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:21.000
How can you be bored
almost immediately?

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.770
This is a historic
Senate impeachment trial,

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.071
not a French New Wave film.

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:26.372
And by the way, we get it,
Truffaut --

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:27.673
life is hard
and death inevitable.

00:03:27.673 --> 00:03:29.508
Would it kill you to throw in

00:03:29.508 --> 00:03:32.111
a guy getting hit in the nuts
with a soccer ball just once?

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:34.980
In fact, at one point,
one of the House managers

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:36.549
prosecuting the case
against Trump,

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:39.619
Jason Crow, a combat veteran,
was laying out in damning detail

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:41.386
just how egregious
Trump's crime was,

00:03:41.386 --> 00:03:44.090
when he noticed that Senators
were leaving the chamber,

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:46.859
and commented on that fact.
-There is a process

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:48.494
for making sure
that U.S. aid money

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:50.597
makes it to the right place,
to the right people.

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:54.600
And, Mr. Chief justice,

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:58.137
I do see a lot of members
moving and taking a break.

00:03:58.137 --> 00:03:59.405
Would we like to take a break
at this time?

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:01.106
I have another
probably 15 minutes.

00:04:01.106 --> 00:04:02.441
-That's insane.

00:04:02.441 --> 00:04:04.377
I mean, in the middle
of laying out damning evidence

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:05.778
against the President
of the United States,

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:08.313
in the middle of an historic
Senate impeachment trial,

00:04:08.313 --> 00:04:11.217
and he had to stop to ask
if the members needed a break.

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:13.052
Can you imagine
an episode of "Law &amp; Order"

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:14.687
where the jury just walks out

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:16.689
during Sam's Waterston's
big speech?

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:19.559
His eyebrows would raise
right off his head.

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:21.260
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:23.362
[ Slide whistle plays ]

00:04:23.362 --> 00:04:26.399
And not only...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:29.802
Not only have senators
been napping, fidgeting,

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:32.104
and leaving the room as evidence
of the President's crime

00:04:32.104 --> 00:04:33.405
is laid out before them,

00:04:33.405 --> 00:04:35.141
some of them are even whining
about the amenities.

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:37.476
For example,
Louisiana Senator Bill Cassidy

00:04:37.476 --> 00:04:38.644
complained to the A.P.,

00:04:38.644 --> 00:04:40.446
there's coffee,
but it's miserable coffee.

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:44.117
Oh, I'm sorry, is the coffee at
the Senate impeachment trial

00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:47.019
not gourmet enough for you?
Should we have George Clooney

00:04:47.019 --> 00:04:49.254
stop by and bring you
an espresso machine?

00:04:49.254 --> 00:04:51.690
[ Cheers and applause ]
And you know who I bet

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:53.893
definitely doesn't care
about the quality of the coffee?

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:56.095
Bernie Sanders.
"I drink black coffee

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:58.197
out of a tin cup
like an old prospector,

00:04:58.197 --> 00:05:01.633
and that's it."
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:01.633 --> 00:05:03.468
"I don't even rinse."

00:05:03.468 --> 00:05:05.704
The Republicans
can't be bothered

00:05:05.704 --> 00:05:07.039
to pay attention
to the evidence,

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:09.074
and neither, it seems,
can Trump's own defense team.

00:05:09.074 --> 00:05:10.810
If you've been watching
the trial in detail,

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.911
you might have noticed
the stark difference

00:05:12.911 --> 00:05:15.314
between the table where the
Democratic House prosecutors

00:05:15.314 --> 00:05:16.849
have been sitting
and the table where

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:18.284
Trump's defense team
has been sitting.

00:05:18.284 --> 00:05:19.986
-You see the counsel table,

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:22.554
that the impeachment managers'
table on the left.

00:05:22.554 --> 00:05:23.723
That's got all the paper on it.

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:26.091
The much cleaner counsel table
on the right

00:05:26.091 --> 00:05:29.695
is the White House defense
counsel for the President.

00:05:29.695 --> 00:05:32.631
You can tell a little bit
about the difference in approach

00:05:32.631 --> 00:05:34.133
from the two sides
simply from looking

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:36.736
at their work environment.
-It's true, the Democrats' table

00:05:36.736 --> 00:05:38.437
looks like it has
actual evidence on it.

00:05:38.437 --> 00:05:39.872
The Trump team's table
looks like

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:41.841
a bus boy
just cleaned it off.

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:43.142
I guess it's not surprising,

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:45.477
given that Trump's desk
is also always so clean.

00:05:45.477 --> 00:05:47.413
I mean, look at that.
He looks like a tourist

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:50.282
taking a photo
on the set of "The West Wing."

00:05:50.282 --> 00:05:52.385
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:52.385 --> 00:05:57.423
"Is this -- Is this the same
phone Martin Sheen used?

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:59.892
This is so cool."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:59.892 --> 00:06:01.594
And even when
they do have papers,

00:06:01.594 --> 00:06:04.096
Trump's defense team usually
doesn't seem prepared

00:06:04.096 --> 00:06:06.132
to actually use them.
I mean, the last time

00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:08.167
a lawyer showed up to Congress
to defend Trump,

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:09.902
he was literally
lugging his documents around

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:11.804
in a grocery-store tote bag.

00:06:11.804 --> 00:06:14.440
Remember that guy from
the House hearing, Steve Castor?

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:17.143
He was either a lawyer or a guy
the Republicans randomly picked

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:19.244
from the frozen aisle
at Whole Foods.

00:06:19.244 --> 00:06:21.481
"Quick, can you come defend
the President from impeachment?"

00:06:21.481 --> 00:06:23.149
"Alright, I guess.
Just let me finish

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:25.184
filling my tote bag
with these Amy's burritos."

00:06:25.184 --> 00:06:26.452
[ Laughter ]

00:06:26.452 --> 00:06:28.120
In fact, Trump's team
is apparently so unwilling

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.890
to listen to the actual
arguments Democrats are making,

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:32.992
that at one point,
Trump's lawyer Jay Sekulow

00:06:32.992 --> 00:06:34.994
went off on an angry tirade

00:06:34.994 --> 00:06:37.530
about something he misheard
during the trial.

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:39.765
Basically,
one of the House prosecutors

00:06:39.765 --> 00:06:43.135
made a reference to FOIA
lawsuits to obtain documents.

00:06:43.135 --> 00:06:46.272
"FOIA" is just an acronym for
"Freedom of Information Act."

00:06:46.272 --> 00:06:47.607
If you're in politics or law

00:06:47.607 --> 00:06:49.074
or are really just a person
who reads the news,

00:06:49.074 --> 00:06:50.509
you've probably
heard that term before.

00:06:50.509 --> 00:06:54.213
But Sekulow thought she said
the words "lawyer lawsuits,"

00:06:54.213 --> 00:06:57.483
which makes no sense at all, and
then he went off about it.

00:06:57.483 --> 00:06:59.819
-The President's lawyers
may suggest

00:06:59.819 --> 00:07:02.455
that the House should have
sought these materials

00:07:02.455 --> 00:07:06.325
in court or
awaited further lawsuits

00:07:06.325 --> 00:07:09.261
under the
Freedom of Information Act --

00:07:09.261 --> 00:07:12.431
AKA, FOIA lawsuits.

00:07:12.431 --> 00:07:15.268
-And by the way...

00:07:15.268 --> 00:07:17.703
lawyer lawsuits?

00:07:17.703 --> 00:07:19.272
[ Laughter ]

00:07:19.272 --> 00:07:21.574
Lawyer lawsuits?

00:07:21.574 --> 00:07:23.776
We're talking
about the impeachment

00:07:23.776 --> 00:07:26.312
of a President of
the United States, duly elected.

00:07:26.312 --> 00:07:29.215
And the members, the managers,

00:07:29.215 --> 00:07:32.318
are complaining
about lawyer lawsuits?

00:07:32.318 --> 00:07:33.486
[ Laughter ]

00:07:33.486 --> 00:07:37.155
The Constitution
allows lawyer lawsuits.

00:07:37.155 --> 00:07:39.458
[ Laughter ]
It's disrespecting

00:07:39.458 --> 00:07:40.826
the Constitution
of the United States

00:07:40.826 --> 00:07:42.428
to even say that
in this chamber --

00:07:42.428 --> 00:07:44.230
lawyer lawsuits.

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.899
-She didn't say it,
because it's not a thing!

00:07:46.899 --> 00:07:50.703
Also, if it was a thing,
why would you be insulted by it?

00:07:50.703 --> 00:07:54.406
Lawyer lawsuits is just a
redundant way to describe a job,

00:07:54.406 --> 00:07:56.875
like "bus-driver bus driving."

00:07:56.875 --> 00:07:59.045
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:59.045 --> 00:08:00.313
"What the [Bleep] did you say?!"

00:08:00.313 --> 00:08:02.781
[ Laughter ]

00:08:02.781 --> 00:08:05.651
Seriously!
How have you never heard...

00:08:05.651 --> 00:08:07.086
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:07.086 --> 00:08:09.488
Have you never heard the term
"FOIA lawsuits" before?

00:08:09.488 --> 00:08:10.856
You're supposed to be a lawyer?

00:08:10.856 --> 00:08:13.259
Did they also pick you
out of line at Whole Foods?

00:08:13.259 --> 00:08:14.627
"Alright, who else here

00:08:14.627 --> 00:08:16.295
wants to defend the President
from impeachment?

00:08:16.295 --> 00:08:18.430
You get a $10 coupon
for an espresso."

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:21.333
And Sekulow isn't
the only Trump defender

00:08:21.333 --> 00:08:23.068
who doesn't seem to know
how the law works.

00:08:23.068 --> 00:08:25.337
Fox News host Jeanine Pirro
lashed out on Twitter

00:08:25.337 --> 00:08:27.807
in the middle of the trial
as House manager Adam Schiff

00:08:27.807 --> 00:08:30.443
was presenting his case,
writing, "Prosecutor Adam Schiff

00:08:30.443 --> 00:08:32.144
says Donald Trump
is not innocent.

00:08:32.144 --> 00:08:33.779
Way to go, Democrats.

00:08:33.779 --> 00:08:36.682
No presumption of innocence.
No constitutional guarantees.

00:08:36.682 --> 00:08:39.318
Welcome to America
under Democrat rule."

00:08:39.318 --> 00:08:42.254
Have you never seen a trial
before?

00:08:42.254 --> 00:08:45.023
Prosecutors
are supposed to argue

00:08:45.023 --> 00:08:47.460
that the defendant is guilty.
That's how it works.

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.061
They don't walk out and say,

00:08:49.061 --> 00:08:50.796
"Ladies and gentlemen
of the jury,

00:08:50.796 --> 00:08:53.032
today we're gonna figure out
some stuff together,

00:08:53.032 --> 00:08:55.334
and however it breaks
is good with me."

00:08:55.334 --> 00:08:57.435
[ Laughter ]

00:08:57.435 --> 00:08:59.471
How do you not know that?

00:08:59.471 --> 00:09:02.774
Your show is literally called
"Justice with Judge Jeanine."

00:09:02.774 --> 00:09:04.910
Are you actually a judge,

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:07.579
or did you just pick that name
because you love alliteration?

00:09:07.579 --> 00:09:09.982
I mean, in that case,
you could have also gone with

00:09:09.982 --> 00:09:11.950
"Janky Jeanine's
Jibber-jabber Junction."

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:13.552
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:13.552 --> 00:09:15.420
You know, while
this was going on,

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:18.224
Trump is at the
World Economic Forum in Davos,

00:09:18.224 --> 00:09:19.492
where he confirmed

00:09:19.492 --> 00:09:21.527
that he was watching
the impeachment proceedings.

00:09:21.527 --> 00:09:23.595
And in the process,
he actually confessed

00:09:23.595 --> 00:09:25.431
to one of the
articles of impeachment,

00:09:25.431 --> 00:09:27.332
obstructing Congress.
During a press conference,

00:09:27.332 --> 00:09:29.602
Trump bragged that his side
was winning the trial

00:09:29.602 --> 00:09:32.705
because he was hiding
all of the evidence

00:09:32.705 --> 00:09:35.441
from House prosecutors.
-We're doing very well.

00:09:35.441 --> 00:09:39.078
I got to watch enough, I thought
our team did a very good job.

00:09:39.078 --> 00:09:40.913
But, honestly,
we have all the material.

00:09:40.913 --> 00:09:42.748
They don't have the material.

00:09:42.748 --> 00:09:44.517
-He literally just confessed.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:44.517 --> 00:09:49.555
Again, the guy confesses more
than a 15-year-old Catholic boy.

00:09:49.555 --> 00:09:51.924
"Forgive me, Father,
for I have sinned

00:09:51.924 --> 00:09:53.325
four times in the bathroom
at home

00:09:53.325 --> 00:09:55.427
and once in the bushes
by cheerleader practice."

00:09:55.427 --> 00:09:58.296
[ Laughter ]
"Also, I'd love to wrap this up

00:09:58.296 --> 00:10:00.066
so I can get home
and sin again."

00:10:00.066 --> 00:10:01.766
[ Laughter ]

00:10:01.766 --> 00:10:03.535
Trump, of course, is only
the third President in history

00:10:03.535 --> 00:10:05.671
to face the prospect of
being removed from office

00:10:05.671 --> 00:10:07.639
by the Senate
in an impeachment trial.

00:10:07.639 --> 00:10:09.641
Now, you might expect
a normal person in that position

00:10:09.641 --> 00:10:10.943
to do everything possible

00:10:10.943 --> 00:10:13.278
to prove that they're competent,
sane, fit for office.

00:10:13.278 --> 00:10:14.780
Instead, here's
the sitting President

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:17.483
of the United States,
amid historic reckoning

00:10:17.483 --> 00:10:19.385
that will stain his name
and presidency forever,

00:10:19.385 --> 00:10:23.388
talking about how Tesla CEO
Elon Musk is good at rockets.

00:10:23.388 --> 00:10:25.457
-Tesla is now worth more
than GM and Ford.

00:10:25.457 --> 00:10:27.192
Do you have comments
on Elon Musk?

00:10:27.192 --> 00:10:28.627
-Well, you have to
give him credit.

00:10:28.627 --> 00:10:31.730
I spoke to him very recently,
and he's also doing the rockets.

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:33.165
He likes rockets.

00:10:33.165 --> 00:10:35.534
And he does good at rockets,
too, by the way.

00:10:35.534 --> 00:10:38.537
-Yeah, yeah, yes, he does.
He does good at rockets.

00:10:38.537 --> 00:10:40.005
[ Laughter ]

00:10:40.005 --> 00:10:42.374
The presidency of Donald Trump
is the closest we'll ever come

00:10:42.374 --> 00:10:45.944
to finding out what it would be
like if Tarzan worked at NASA.

00:10:45.944 --> 00:10:48.980
"Ground control to Tarzan,
What's your status?"

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:51.817
"Space cold for Tarzan,
but Tarzan good at rockets."

00:10:51.817 --> 00:10:53.351
[ Laughter ]

00:10:53.351 --> 00:10:54.987
What we've seen
once again this week is

00:10:54.987 --> 00:10:56.855
that Trump and his lawyers
have no defense

00:10:56.855 --> 00:10:58.223
for his obviously corrupt
behavior,

00:10:58.223 --> 00:10:59.891
which is why
their desks are empty

00:10:59.891 --> 00:11:01.893
and their Republican allies
are leaving the chamber

00:11:01.893 --> 00:11:02.995
and ignoring the evidence.

00:11:02.995 --> 00:11:04.930
Even if he's acquitted
by the Senate,

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:07.266
Trump may very well spend
the rest of his life in court,

00:11:07.266 --> 00:11:09.534
dealing with legal challenges
and indictments,

00:11:09.534 --> 00:11:11.003
or as they're
technically known...

00:11:11.003 --> 00:11:12.271
-Lawyer lawsuits.

00:11:12.271 --> 00:11:14.206
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:11:14.206 --> 00:11:16.575
[ "A Closer Look" theme plays ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

